A run printed "all 1 CONFIRMED (of 1 claim(s))" (the claim holds: no
flow found) and then "§3a walk verdicts for those findings: confirmed 3"
(a secret reached a sink): one word for opposite facts. Owner ruling
2026-10-25: do the full rename.

WALK_VERDICT_CONFIRMED / WALK_VERDICT_UNCONFIRMED ("confirmed" /
"unconfirmed") are WALK_VERDICT_REACHED / WALK_VERDICT_REFUTED
("reached" / "refuted"), in every evidence row's walk_verdict /
walk_verdict_values and the dataflow_coverage.walk_verdicts keys.
"refuted" matches the existing refuted_flows key. The verify-claims
envelope goes 2.6 -> 3.0, breaking under the module's own version
policy, as 2.0 was. The spec, VERIFY-CLAIMS-SCOPE.md, ADR-0017 and
ADR-0052 use the new names; measurement write-ups keep the names their
runs printed. The spec's io-boundaries version line (2.4) is corrected
to 2.5.

No reader to keep compatible: nothing in the tree deserialises a
TaintFlowFinding or reads walk_verdict out of a cached artifact
(bakeoff-deep reads claim verdicts only; the measure-* scripts pass
walk_verdict through as a key).

Addresses WI-bujum.

